==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|schicken||to outfit oneself, fit in, arrange appropriately}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*skikkijaną||to order, send}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*skeg-||to jump, spring}}; representing the causative of {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|geschehen|geschehen, geschēn|to happen, rush}} from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|giskehan||to happen}} from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*skehaną||to run, move quickly}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*skek-||to run, jump, spring}}. Akin to {{cog|enm|skekken||to send forth}}, {{cog|ang|scēon||to happen}}, ''schie-'' in {{cog|nl|schielijk||hasty}}. More at {{m|en|chic}}.

